# Zealakit Pattern Input conventions

- `@zealakit/pattern-input-core` is framework-independent and has two entries: `.` (pure: state
  machines, parsers, prop getters) and `./dom` (the shared DOM binding). Never import React / Vue /
  Svelte from it, and never import `./dom` from the pure entry.
- Adapters (`vanilla`, `react`, `vue`, `svelte`) depend on core with `workspace:^`; core depends
  on no adapter. Keep the dependency graph acyclic.
- The `.` entry must stay DOM-free: `tsconfig.pure.json` typechecks it with `lib: ["ES2022"]`.
  Any `window`/`document`/`Element` use in `packages/core/src` outside `src/dom/` fails checks.
- SSR safety: no `window` / `document` access at module init or during render. DOM work belongs in
  the `./dom` binding or framework lifecycle hooks.
- Formatting and parsing are pure over `(rawValue, options)`; the caret is sticky relative to the
  raw value, never an index into the formatted string.
- IME composition commits exactly once at `compositionend`. Never format, reject, or commit state
  mid-composition.
- The `./dom` binding is the only writer of `el.value` and selection. Framework adapters must not
  bind `value` reactively.
- Do not ship default CSS, class names, themes, or design tokens. Styling is the consumer's job.
- Never wrap or replace a plain-text `<input>`. Fields attach behavior to consumer-owned elements,
  or render only the specialized field's own element(s).
- No bundled schema validation: validity comes from the field's own parsing plus optional consumer
  callbacks.
- New core primitives ship with focused tests (`pnpm test`). Do not add a second test framework.
- Do not export unimplemented APIs, placeholder components, or fake implementations.
- TypeScript only: `type` aliases, `import type`, strict mode, ESM with `.js` specifiers, kebab-case
  file names, no `any` in exported signatures.
- Build order matters: core emits `dist` first; adapters resolve core through its package exports.
  Run `pnpm build` before `pnpm typecheck`.
- Verify with `pnpm check` (build + typecheck + test + lint) before reporting work as done. Run
  `pnpm readme:check` after README changes and the relevant example builds when those areas change.
- `examples/` are integration/smoke-test projects only. Product documentation lives only in the
  root and package READMEs (EN, VI, CN); there is no `docs/` folder and no separate docs app.
- Load the compact `.agents/skills/pattern-input/SKILL.md` before code, test, docs, or release work,
  and `.agents/skills/readme-system/SKILL.md` before touching any README.
- Update the READMEs, `.agents/AGENTS.md`, and `.agents/skills/pattern-input/SKILL.md` together when
  architecture, package boundaries, commands, or documented workflows change.
